    "https://vsc.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/VTSU/job/Williston-VT/Assistant-Professor_R-2026382": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nVermont State University (VTSU), Williston/St. Albans campus invites applicants for a full-time faculty position in the Department of Nursing for the academic year 2026-2027, teaching across the Practical Nursing (PN) Program and Associate Degree in Nursing (ASN) Program. Qualified candidates will be offered a tenure-track position or a one-year terminal contract, renewable for three years, based on the individual's years of full-time clinical nursing experience and years of full-time teaching in an accredited nursing program. Each faculty member in the Department of Nursing is responsible for: 1. Contributing to the professional learning environment in the classroom and in clinical rotations. 2. Encouraging student learning and retention, consistent with the student learning outcomes and course objectives, nurturing an environment focused on providing the highest quality of care to patients. 3. Evaluating student acquisition of nursing competence. 4. Participating in the implementation, evaluation, and revision of the nursing curriculum and relevant policies. 5. Serving as an academic adviser to students across the programs. 6. Participating in assigned roles in the Department of Nursing standing committees. 7. Demonstrating continued professional development in the areas of nursing and nursing education commensurate with assigned roles. 8. Collaborating with healthcare partners across the state of Vermont. 9. Complying with the policies outlined by the Vermont State College system, Vermont State University, and the Department of Nursing. Specific Criteria for this position include: 1. An unencumbered Registered Nurse license allowing practice in Vermont. 2. Masters of Science in Nursing 3. A minimum of two years full-time, or the equivalent of, acute care nursing experience. 4. Commitment to the mission and vision of Vermont State University and the Department of Nursing. 5. Commitment to the integration of technology, including simulation across the curriculum. 6. Knowledge of processes related to NLN-CNEA Accreditation. 7. Occasional travel to other campus sites and/or clinical agencies in the region. Salary:  Based on qualifications and experience as defined by the VSC-VSCFF Bargaining Unit Agreement   Application Information:  Applicants interested in applying  must submit a Cover Letter, Resume/CV, and Unofficial College Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired).  Applications will be accepted until position is filled or by date specified. However, applications received after the initial screening will be considered at the discretion of Vermont State University. VTSU strongly encourages applications from members of ethnic minority groups and other under-represented backgrounds. VTSU is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual because of race, color, religion, ancestry, place of birth, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, age or veteran status, or against a qualified individual with a disability, or any other person whose status is protected under local, state or federal laws. In compliance with ADA requirements, we will make reasonable accommodations for the known disability of an otherwise qualified applicant. For more information visit the VSC system website www.vsc.edu/agreements-personnel-handbook/ All full-time and some part-time positions are subject to a criminal background check. Any offer of employment is conditional upon successful completion of these checks.   Scheduled Hours Weekly: 37.5 Budgeted Wage for this Position: $57,500 based on qualifications and experience as defined by the VSC-VSCFF Bargaining Unit Agreement. Exempt Status: Exempt Grade: F01 Job Posting Responsibilities: Unit Determination: Full-Time Faculty -VSC Faculty Federation"
    },
    "https://vsc.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/VTSU/job/Williston-VT/Clinical-Associate---Paramedic-Education_R-2026498": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate - Paramedic Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\nPart time\n\nClinical Associate - Paramedic Education Supervises practical application of theory in assigned clinical settings. Demonstrates care and procedures. Fulfill various instructional clinical roles in clinical settings as designed by the Program Director. Works in collaboration with the Program Director, Medical Director, Clinical Outplacement Coordinator, and Simulation Director to ensure effective education and accurate evaluation of students. Characteristic Duties & Responsibilities Supervision, education, and evaluation of students as assigned by the Program Director Review and abide by student handbook policies Attend scheduled in-service meetings and department meetings as scheduled Collaboration with faculty and staff to ensure that syllabi are being followed, learning objectives are being met, and formative and summative evaluation strategies are employed to enhance the learning process Communicate effectively with students, staff, and faculty Work outside regular business hours might be expected Occasional in-state travel may be anticipated Supervision Received General supervision is received from the Program Director, Paramedicine Education Supervision Exercised None Bachelor's degree preferred and/or 2-4 years of experience in the paramedic field or a combination of education and experience from which comparable knowledge and skills are acquired. A Vermont Paramedic License or Vermont Registered Nurse License with EMS experience is required. Knowledge of course content being delivered Excellent verbal, interpersonal, and written communication skills Strong analytical, problem-solving, and flexible decision-making capabilities Team player with the ability to multitask in a fast-paced work environment Ability to work under strict deadlines in a fast-paced environment Ability to ensure considerable walking, standing, and lifting while instructing/supervising students Ability to deal effectively with and represent the College to a broad range of individuals and groups within and outside of the College All required immunizations must be up to date Valid Vermont Driver's license This general outline illustrates the type of work which characterizes the job classification. It is not an all-encompassing statement of the specific duties, responsibilities, and qualifications of individual positions assigned to the classification. Scheduled Hours Weekly: 28 Budgeted Wage for this Position: Certificate: $25/hr Associate $30/hr, Bachelor $35/hr Master $40/hr Master with 5 years, or Doctorate $45 Exempt Status: Exempt Grade: T01 Job Posting Responsibilities:"
